- const aiFoundryLayer={icon:'🏭',eyebrow:'Admin → AI Agent Foundry',name:'AI Agent Foundry',blurb:'Bring your own Anthropic, OpenAI-compatible or Google Gemini key - Lanesra never resells inference - then build on it: a conversational Chat Assistant with real tool access, and a full AI Agent Foundry where an Administrator defines named agents with a persona, a per-tool Actions checklist, persistent Memory, a shared Skills library, guardrails, and delegation to other agents. Chain agents into a deterministic Pipeline - sequential, consensus, or a peer-review loop - and fire it manually, on a schedule, from a webhook, or as a new Workflow Automation action, with human-in-the-loop approval gates and OTLP tracing on any run. A real Evaluation Harness grades an agent\'s answers against golden test cases - every run lands in one unified history. Every agent also carries a real Draft → Test → Published → Deprecated → Disabled version lifecycle - a Published version is an immutable snapshot of exactly what ran, and can declare a JSON-schema Structured Output contract checked automatically with one repair attempt - and a durable, workspace-wide Approval inbox generalizes "something needs a human decision" beyond a single Pipeline step.'};
- const policyLayer={icon:'🛡️',eyebrow:'Admin → AI Agents → Policy Engine',name:'Toolboxes & Policy Engine',blurb:'Every tool an agent can call - native, Connector-bridged or MCP-sourced alike - carries a real risk classification (Read, Low-Write, Write, External-Action, Destructive, Privileged), overridable per tool name from a Tool Registry. A workspace-default or per-agent Policy sets a require-approval threshold and an outright blocklist on top of that classification. None of this is a second enforcement path: it formalizes the exact same tool-dispatch point every agent call already runs through into named stages - schema → permission → policy → approval → execute → audit - a Tool-Call Firewall, not a bolted-on filter.'};
- const graphLayer={icon:'⌗',eyebrow:'Admin → AI Agent Foundry → Agent Teams',name:'Shared Execution Graph & Agent Teams',blurb:'A durable, checkpointed graph runtime underlies every Workflow and Orchestration Pipeline - Trigger, Condition, Action, Agent, Router, Parallel Split, Join, Approval, Delay, Transform, Loop and End nodes, with a real per-node run trace and resumable execution: kill the app mid-run and it picks up exactly where it left off. A sequential Pipeline, a consensus vote and a peer-review loop are each just a specific graph shape on this same engine, proven byte-for-byte against the pre-migration code path. Admin → AI Agent Foundry → Agent Teams exposes it directly: a free-form drag-and-drop canvas to wire agents, conditions and approval gates into a named team, with the same Draft → Publish lifecycle and a Runs tab to start, approve, reject or resume a live run.'};
- const memoryLayer={icon:'🧠',eyebrow:'Admin → AI Agent Foundry → Knowledge & Memory',name:'Memory Architecture & Document RAG',blurb:'Beyond an agent\'s own persistent Memory document, three itemized memory types - Session, Working and Entity - are written and read by real remember/get_memory tool calls mid-conversation, each scoped, sourced, confidence-scored and TTL\'d, with a Policy Engine check gating what may persist. Document RAG turns curated Knowledge Sources into real, chunked, embedded content any agent can cite: a search_knowledge tool call always returns a source citation alongside the answer, built on the same embeddings provider and Vector Search this platform already ships - not a second, parallel pipeline.'};
- const mcpLayer={icon:'⌁',eyebrow:'Admin → LLM & MCP',name:'MCP Server, CLI & Client',blurb:'A stateless POST /mcp endpoint speaks the Model Context Protocol over JSON-RPC 2.0 - the same protocol Claude Desktop and most IDE coding agents use - securely exposing your Custom Objects, records and business logic to any MCP-capable client, authenticated with the same scoped API keys the REST API already uses. A companion CLI gives humans and shell scripts that same REST API access without an agent in the loop. The same protocol also runs in reverse from Admin → AI Agent Foundry → Agent Teams → MCP Servers: connect an external MCP server as a governed Connection, discover its tools with a real initialize + tools/list handshake, and opt individual tools in as agent-callable - read-only by default, with the identical two-level write gate and Tool-Call Firewall trace every other tool already gets.'};
